            <div class="flex items-center gap-3"><span class="w-12 text-[13px] font-medium text-[#111827]">West</span><i class="race-bar h-3 rounded-full bg-red-400" style="width:41%; animation-delay:.2s"></i><span class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-red-500">declined</span></div>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3"><span class="w-12 text-[13px] text-navy-600">South</span><i class="race-bar h-3 rounded-full" style="width:72%; background: linear-gradient(90deg,#9bd600,#76B900); animation-delay:.3s"></i></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <style>
      @keyframes race-in { 0%, 14% { transform: scaleX(0); opacity: .3; } 24%, 100% { transform: scaleX(1); opacity: 1; } }
      .race-bar { display: block; transform-origin: left; animation: race-in 7s ease-out infinite; }
      @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .race-bar { animation: none; } }
    </style>
    <p class="mt-10 text-center font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-[#9CA3AF]">Illustrative example with made-up data. Both paths start together.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 sm:py-24 lg:px-8" aria-labelledby="gu-alt-heading">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl">
    <div class="mb-14 max-w-3xl" data-reveal>
      <span class="mb-5 inline-flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-[#5a9100]"><span class="h-px w-8 bg-[#5a9100]"></span>Alternatives</span>
      <h2 id="gu-alt-heading" class="text-[32px] font-medium leading-[1.12] tracking-tight text-[#111827] sm:text-[42px]">Chat, fixed screens, or generative UI?</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 md:items-stretch" data-reveal>
      <div class="py-2 md:py-8 md:pr-10"><div class="relative"><h3 class="text-[24px] font-medium tracking-tight text-[#111827]">Chat reply</h3><p class="mt-1 mb-5 text-[14px] leading-snug text-[#6B7280]">Best when the answer is genuinely prose.</p><dl><div class="border-t border-navy-100 py-3.5"><dt class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-[#9CA3AF]">Output</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-[15.5px] leading-snug text-[#111827]">Text</dd></div><div class="border-t border-navy-100 py-3.5"><dt class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-[#9CA3AF]">Who designed it</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-[15.5px] leading-snug text-[#111827]">Nobody</dd></div><div class="border-t border-navy-100 py-3.5"><dt class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-[#9CA3AF]">Unanticipated asks</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-[15.5px] leading-snug text-[#111827]">Yes, as text</dd></div><div class="border-t border-navy-100 py-3.5"><dt class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-[#9CA3AF]">Act on the answer in place</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-[15.5px] leading-snug text-[#111827]">No</dd></div><div class="border-t border-navy-100 py-3.5"><dt class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-[#9CA3AF]">Layout</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-[15.5px] leading-snug text-[#111827]">n/a</dd></div><div class="border-t border-navy-100 py-3.5"><dt class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-[#9CA3AF]">Cost per new view</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-[15.5px] leading-snug text-[#111827]">None</dd></div></dl></div></div>
      <div class="py-2 md:border-l md:border-navy-100 md:px-10 md:py-8"><div class="relative"><h3 class="text-[24px] font-medium tracking-tight text-[#111827]">Fixed screens</h3><p class="mt-1 mb-5 text-[14px] leading-snug text-[#6B7280]">Best when the task is known and repeated.</p><dl><div class="border-t border-navy-100 py-3.5"><dt class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-[#9CA3AF]">Output</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-[15.5px] leading-snug text-[#111827]">Interface</dd></div><div class="border-t border-navy-100 py-3.5"><dt class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-[#9CA3AF]">Who designed it</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-[15.5px] leading-snug text-[#111827]">A developer, in advance</dd></div><div class="border-t border-navy-100 py-3.5"><dt class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-[#9CA3AF]">Unanticipated asks</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-[15.5px] leading-snug text-[#111827]">No</dd></div><div class="border-t border-navy-100 py-3.5"><dt class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-[#9CA3AF]">Act on the answer in place</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-[15.5px] leading-snug text-[#111827]">Yes</dd></div><div class="border-t border-navy-100 py-3.5"><dt class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-[#9CA3AF]">Layout</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-[15.5px] leading-snug text-[#111827]">Completely predictable</dd></div><div class="border-t border-navy-100 py-3.5"><dt class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-[#9CA3AF]">Cost per new view</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-[15.5px] leading-snug text-[#111827]">A sprint</dd></div></dl></div></div>
      <div class="relative overflow-hidden rounded-[28px] bg-navy-950 p-8 md:-my-5 md:p-10"><div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0" aria-hidden="true" style="background: radial-gradient(ellipse 80% 50% at 100% 0%, rgba(118,185,0,.28) 0%, transparent 60%);"></div><div class="relative"><span class="mb-3 inline-block rounded-full bg-[#76B900]/20 px-3 py-1 font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-[#9bd600]">What we build</span><h3 class="text-[24px] font-medium tracking-tight text-white">Generative UI</h3><p class="mt-1 mb-5 text-[14px] leading-snug text-[#9bd600]">Best for the long tail nobody anticipated.</p><dl><div class="border-t border-white/10 py-3.5"><dt class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-white/40">Output</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-[15.5px] leading-snug text-white">Interface</dd></div><div class="border-t border-white/10 py-3.5"><dt class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-white/40">Who designed it</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-[15.5px] leading-snug text-white">Assembled at runtime from your components</dd></div><div class="border-t border-white/10 py-3.5"><dt class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-white/40">Unanticipated asks</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-[15.5px] leading-snug text-white">Yes, as interface</dd></div><div class="border-t border-white/10 py-3.5"><dt class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-white/40">Act on the answer in place</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-[15.5px] leading-snug text-white">Yes</dd></div><div class="border-t border-white/10 py-3.5"><dt class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-white/40">Layout</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-[15.5px] leading-snug text-white">Predictable within the component registry</dd></div><div class="border-t border-white/10 py-3.5"><dt class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-white/40">Cost per new view</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-[15.5px] leading-snug text-white">None</dd></div></dl></div></div>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-12 max-w-3xl text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]">Fixed screens remain the right answer for most of a mature product, and we would not propose replacing them. Generative UI earns its place on the long tail: the one-off views that never justified a build.</p>
  </div>
</section>

{# ============ HOW WE BUILD IT ============ #}
<section class="relative overflow-hidden bg-navy-950 px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 sm:py-24 lg:px-8 lg:py-28" aria-labelledby="gu-build-heading">
  <div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0" aria-hidden="true" style="background: radial-gradient(ellipse 55% 60% at 0% 0%, rgba(118,185,0,0.16) 0%, transparent 60%), radial-gradient(ellipse 45% 55% at 100% 100%, rgba(87,119,130,0.22) 0%, transparent 60%);"></div>
  <div class="relative mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[0.75fr_1.25fr] lg:gap-20">
    <div class="lg:sticky lg:top-28 lg:self-start" data-reveal>
      <span class="mb-5 inline-flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-[#9bd600]"><span class="h-px w-8 bg-[#9bd600]"></span>How we build it</span>
      <h2 id="gu-build-heading" class="text-[34px] font-medium leading-[1.1] tracking-tight text-white sm:text-[46px]">The model is the small part.</h2>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-md text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-white/60">The work is mostly in your component layer: what exists, what is allowed, and how it is tested. Get those right and the model has very little room to go wrong.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="border-b border-white/10" data-reveal>
      <li class="group relative grid grid-cols-[4.5rem_1fr] items-start gap-x-5 border-t border-white/10 py-7 transition-colors duration-300 hover:bg-white/[0.03] sm:grid-cols-[7rem_1fr_auto] sm:gap-x-8 sm:py-9">
        <span class="text-[56px] font-semibold leading-none tracking-tight text-transparent transition-all duration-300 group-hover:text-[#9bd600] sm:text-[84px]" style="-webkit-text-stroke: 1.5px #76B900;">01</span>
        <div class="max-w-xl"><h3 class="text-[22px] font-medium leading-snug tracking-tight text-white sm:text-[26px]">Your component library</h3><p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-white/55 transition-colors group-hover:text-white/80">A component library worth generating from: React components with clear props, in reasonable shape.</p></div>
        <span class="mt-2 hidden text-[26px] text-white/20 transition-all duration-300 group-hover:translate-x-2 group-hover:text-[#9bd600] sm:block" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
      </li>
      <li class="group relative grid grid-cols-[4.5rem_1fr] items-start gap-x-5 border-t border-white/10 py-7 transition-colors duration-300 hover:bg-white/[0.03] sm:grid-cols-[7rem_1fr_auto] sm:gap-x-8 sm:py-9">
        <span class="text-[56px] font-semibold leading-none tracking-tight text-transparent transition-all duration-300 group-hover:text-[#9bd600] sm:text-[84px]" style="-webkit-text-stroke: 1.5px #76B900;">02</span>
        <div class="max-w-xl"><h3 class="text-[22px] font-medium leading-snug tracking-tight text-white sm:text-[26px]">One surface first</h3><p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-white/55 transition-colors group-hover:text-white/80">The screen users complain about most, built beside your current UI so you can compare the two directly.</p></div>
        <span class="mt-2 hidden text-[26px] text-white/20 transition-all duration-300 group-hover:translate-x-2 group-hover:text-[#9bd600] sm:block" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
      </li>
      <li class="group relative grid grid-cols-[4.5rem_1fr] items-start gap-x-5 border-t border-white/10 py-7 transition-colors duration-300 hover:bg-white/[0.03] sm:grid-cols-[7rem_1fr_auto] sm:gap-x-8 sm:py-9">
        <span class="text-[56px] font-semibold leading-none tracking-tight text-transparent transition-all duration-300 group-hover:text-[#9bd600] sm:text-[84px]" style="-webkit-text-stroke: 1.5px #76B900;">03</span>
        <div class="max-w-xl"><h3 class="text-[22px] font-medium leading-snug tracking-tight text-white sm:text-[26px]">Data and permissions</h3><p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-white/55 transition-colors group-hover:text-white/80">Your existing endpoints and permission model, honoured exactly. There is no second access path.</p></div>
        <span class="mt-2 hidden text-[26px] text-white/20 transition-all duration-300 group-hover:translate-x-2 group-hover:text-[#9bd600] sm:block" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
      </li>
      <li class="group relative grid grid-cols-[4.5rem_1fr] items-start gap-x-5 border-t border-white/10 py-7 transition-colors duration-300 hover:bg-white/[0.03] sm:grid-cols-[7rem_1fr_auto] sm:gap-x-8 sm:py-9">
        <span class="text-[56px] font-semibold leading-none tracking-tight text-transparent transition-all duration-300 group-hover:text-[#9bd600] sm:text-[84px]" style="-webkit-text-stroke: 1.5px #76B900;">04</span>
        <div class="max-w-xl"><h3 class="text-[22px] font-medium leading-snug tracking-tight text-white sm:text-[26px]">Registry and schemas</h3><p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-white/55 transition-colors group-hover:text-white/80">Approved components by name, with every prop checked against a schema before anything renders.</p></div>
        <span class="mt-2 hidden text-[26px] text-white/20 transition-all duration-300 group-hover:translate-x-2 group-hover:text-[#9bd600] sm:block" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
      </li>
      <li class="group relative grid grid-cols-[4.5rem_1fr] items-start gap-x-5 border-t border-white/10 py-7 transition-colors duration-300 hover:bg-white/[0.03] sm:grid-cols-[7rem_1fr_auto] sm:gap-x-8 sm:py-9">
        <span class="text-[56px] font-semibold leading-none tracking-tight text-transparent transition-all duration-300 group-hover:text-[#9bd600] sm:text-[84px]" style="-webkit-text-stroke: 1.5px #76B900;">05</span>
        <div class="max-w-xl"><h3 class="text-[22px] font-medium leading-snug tracking-tight text-white sm:text-[26px]">Real-request tests</h3><p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-white/55 transition-colors group-hover:text-white/80">Ten or twenty real requests become the regression suite, which is how you test an interface that changes every time.</p></div>
        <span class="mt-2 hidden text-[26px] text-white/20 transition-all duration-300 group-hover:translate-x-2 group-hover:text-[#9bd600] sm:block" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

{# ============ FIT / NOT FIT ============ #}
<section class="px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 sm:py-20 lg:px-8" aria-labelledby="gu-fit-heading">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl">
    <h2 id="gu-fit-heading" class="sr-only">When to use it and when not to</h2>
    <div class="grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2" data-reveal-stagger>
      <div class="rounded-[28px] border border-[#76B900]/30 bg-[#76B900]/[0.06] p-7 sm:p-9">
        <span class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-[#3d6600]">A good fit</span>
        <ul class="mt-5 space-y-3 text-[16px] text-[#111827]">
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[#76B900]">&#10003;</span>The long tail of questions no fixed screen covers</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[#76B900]">&#10003;</span>Reports people cannot find or cannot ask for in your schema</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[#76B900]">&#10003;</span>Long forms where most fields do not apply to most cases</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[#76B900]">&#10003;</span>Assistants that should do the task, not describe it</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-[28px] border border-navy-100 bg-white p-7 sm:p-9">
        <span class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-[#9CA3AF]">A poor fit</span>
        <ul class="mt-5 space-y-3 text-[16px] text-[#111827]">
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-navy-300">&#8212;</span>Well-understood, repeated flows like checkout, where a fixed screen is better</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-navy-300">&#8212;</span>Screens where the exact wording or layout is fixed by regulation</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-navy-300">&#8212;</span>Tasks that are already one good screen</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-5 text-[14px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]">Fixed screens stay better wherever the task is understood and repeated. That is most of a mature product.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

